{# Go exemplary fixture template — emits one
adapters/{bidder}/{bidder}test/exemplary/{descriptive-name}.json file
per source-side scenario.

Go's flat fixture shape collapses Java's IT 4-file split (auction-
request, auction-response, bid-request, bid-response) into a single
JSON file with `httpCalls[]` and `expectedBidResponses[]` arrays.

The Go fixture format is:

  {
    "expectedRequest": <publisher-side BidRequest BidRequest>,
    "httpCalls": [
      {
        "expectedRequest": { uri, body },
        "mockResponse": { status, body }
      }
    ],
    "expectedBidResponses": [{ currency, bids: [{ bid, type }] }]
  }

Inputs:
  ctx.expected_request   : dict  — the BidRequest the harness feeds to MakeRequests
  ctx.http_calls         : list[dict]  — per outgoing HTTP call; each:
      uri      : str  — the bidder endpoint URL the adapter resolved
      body     : dict  — the JSON body the adapter sent (typically a BidRequest)
      status   : int  — mock response status (200, 204, 400, ...)
      response : dict|null  — mock response body (BidResponse or null for 204)
  ctx.expected_bids      : list[dict]  — per BidderBid result; each:
      bid      : dict  — the openrtb response.Bid
      type     : str   — "banner" | "video" | "audio" | "native"
  ctx.expected_currency  : str  — typically "USD"

For supplemental (error-path) fixtures, the same template applies but
expected_bids is typically empty and httpCalls returns a non-200 status
or malformed body. The SKILL Step 5 emits those into
adapters/{bidder}/{bidder}test/supplemental/.
#}
{
  "expectedRequest": {{ ctx.expected_request | tojson }},
  "httpCalls": [
{% for call in ctx.http_calls %}
    {
      "expectedRequest": {
        "uri": {{ call.uri | tojson }},
        "body": {{ call.body | tojson }}
      },
      "mockResponse": {
        "status": {{ call.status }}{% if call.response %},
        "body": {{ call.response | tojson }}{% endif %}

      }
    }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
  ],
  "expectedBidResponses": [
{% if ctx.expected_bids %}
    {
      "currency": {{ ctx.expected_currency | tojson }},
      "bids": [
{% for eb in ctx.expected_bids %}
        {
          "bid": {{ eb.bid | tojson }},
          "type": {{ eb.type | tojson }}
        }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
      ]
    }
{% endif %}
  ]
}
